  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits severe upward bias when recent history shows a strong positive spike (e.g., >73) followed by neutral sentiment; true outcomes often reverse sharply downward within the first 5 days.",
    "Forecast fails to capture immediate mean reversion after high volatility spikes, instead projecting a linear trend that ignores the subsequent crash pattern seen in true outcomes.",
    "Sentiment history of -1.00 or 1.00 correlates with sudden price breaks; model forecasts remain static and do not adjust trajectory based on these sentiment extremes.",
    "When recent history is volatile (range >65-74), the model's 30-day forecast should be capped at the current price plus a small buffer, rather than extrapolating linearly to +10-15 points.",
    "True outcomes frequently show a 'spike and drop' pattern where the first few days of the forecast period are significantly higher than the average of the last 3 days of history."
  ]
}
